Sir Slash started off fairly clumsy with a Dex of 9 and had a habit of
walking into doors and falling off ponies.  But then on the 2nd level
magic happened.. he found a wand of wishing.  2 charges.  1st wish was
for 2 blessed scrolls of charging, 2nd was for blessed +3 grey dragon
scale mail (got it at +3).  charged back up and I got my amulet of
reflection, speed boots (+0) and a bag of holding.  wrested wish went
to a blessed +3 rustproof helm of brilliance (got it at +0).

Honestly, this made the game pretty much a cake walk.  No real close
calls to speak of.

Problems:  I forgot to get candles in mine town so I had to go back
after I got the candelabrum, then I had no gold to pay for them so I
grabbed all the candles in the shop and teleported out to the stairs
and back up.  Then for some reason I forgot to get the amulet of
yendor (forgive me, it's been a couple of years since I made it this
far) and I went back up to level 1 with the candles, book and bell.
When I hit < to go up and it asked me I realized something was wrong.
I had narrowly missed getting an ascension by my stupidity (isn't that
always the way though?).

Went back down, got to the vibrating square and lit my candles, read
the book (summoning undead) and rang the bell.  Hmm.. that didn't
work.. went to google, read the correct procedure and tried again.
Opened the vault of the dead and really just walked down and killed
everyone to get the amulet.

Wizard showed up too many times and I got sent back too many times to
count.  By the time I made it to level 1 I was ready to go.  I went up
and got lucky on earth and tunneled right to the portal (forgot to get
gold detection scrolls)

Air and Fire were ok, I wrote some scrolls and used a wand of secret
door detection to help out.  Water sucked since the portal kept
moving.. but I got lucky and found it and made my way to the astral
plane.

2nd altar was the trick.  I stayed there for a bit slaying from the
safety of the narrow entryway, but soon grew bored and went ahead and
sacrificed the amulet.  (no need to go for one of those 12million
point scores or something weird.  That's why I didn't tunnel out
Gehenom (or all the other levels like I have in the past) I just
navigated the mazes and teleported where I could to jump from stairway
to stairway.

